1d3cca16fcd2,frozen_450,/Users/baiyixin/Downloads/1d3cca16fcd2.pdf,/Users/baiyixin/Documents/Survey - design knowledge/expanded_pdf_corpus_459_20260811/1d3cca16fcd2.pdf,dc974204eb6f71a551438497d31db16155530caac939cf66bfd3b060047cdc50,True,20,"Legitimating design: a sociology of knowledge account of the ﬁeld Lucila Carvalho and Andy Dong, Design Lab, Faculty of Architecture, Design and Planning, Wilkinson Building (G04), University of Sydney, 148 City Road, Sydney NSW 2006, Australia Karl Maton, Department of Sociology & Social Policy, Faculty of Arts, University of Sydney, Sydney NSW 2006, Australia This paper presents a sociology of knowledge approach to describe disciplines in the ﬁeld of design. We show how the approach casts the nature of knowledge in design disciplines as based upon socially agreed criteria for what constitutes the realization of legitimate knowledge. Interviews with designers and analyses of professional and pedagogic discourse about design are used to illustrate how the approach reveals the diﬀerences in what kind of design knowledge is valued, cultivated, and emphasised within a discipline. By placing a sociological lens on knowledge in design, we aim to suggest a language by which what counts as de"
