3c0bd4608ae9,frozen_450,/Users/baiyixin/Downloads/3c0bd4608ae9.pdf,/Users/baiyixin/Documents/Survey - design knowledge/expanded_pdf_corpus_459_20260811/3c0bd4608ae9.pdf,994e97fe2d36dd7c8dfb50cfd642913ec455ddcdd53a0b26f12e4e5020984919,True,13,"Copyright ©IAARR, 2012-2016: www.afrrevjo.net/stech | Indexed African Journals Online: www.ajol.info 1 STECH VOL 5 (1) FEBRUARY, 2016 Vol. 5 (1), S/No11, February, 2016: 1-13 ISSN: 2225-8590 (Print) ISSN 2227-5452 (Online) DOI: http://dx.doi.org/10.4314/stech.v5i1.1 Reflections on Architecture Design Education: The Integrated Design Paradigm Bashier, Fathi Department of Architecture, Urban Planning & Development Faculty of Engineering & Technology, Wollega University, Ethiopia Email: fatibashier@yahoo.com; fatibashier@gmail.com Mob: +251 9 368 83917 (Ethiopia), +249 910517774 (Sudan) Abstract Studies have recently discussed the failure of traditional design in the studio to develop a rational approach based on systematic methods and objective knowledge. They agree that such an approach is incompatible with the complexity of modern design problems and recognize the need to replace it with a disciplinary approach in order to meet the challenges of modern design. Most critics attribute th"
