97b253588409,frozen_450,/Users/baiyixin/Downloads/97b253588409.pdf,/Users/baiyixin/Documents/Survey - design knowledge/expanded_pdf_corpus_459_20260811/97b253588409.pdf,2a7ad1c643de17771806072711bef3b8cb641b1bf9a0a3384fbb021ea1d72943,True,7,"AN INFORMATION SYSTEMS DESIGN THEORY FOR WEB-BASEDEDUCATIONDavid JonesFaculty of Informatics andCommunicationCentral Queensland UniversityRockhampton, Australia, 4701d.jones@cqu.edu.au+61-7-4930-9856 (phone)+61-7-4930-9729 (fax) Shirley GregorSchool of Business and InformationManagementAustralian National UniversityCanberra, Australia, 0200shirley.gregor@anu.edu.au+61-2-6125-3749 (phone)+61-2-6125-5005 (fax) Teresa LynchFaculty of Informatics andCommunicationCentral Queensland UniversityRockhamptonAustralia, 4701t.lynch@cqu.edu.au+61-7-4930-9027 (phone)+61-7-4930-9729 (fax) ABSTRACTAn Information Systems Design Theory (ISDT) is aprescriptive theory that offers theory-based principles thatcan guide practitioners in the design of effectiveInformation Systems and set an agenda for on-goingresearch. This paper introduces the origins of the ISDTconcept and describes one ISDT for Web-basedEducation (WBE). The paper shows how this ISDT has,over the last seven years, produced a WBE Information"
97b32465f821,frozen_450,/Users/baiyixin/Documents/Survey - design knowledge/pdfs_ready_for_drive_upload/97b32465f821.pdf,/Users/baiyixin/Documents/Survey - design knowledge/expanded_pdf_corpus_459_20260811/97b32465f821.pdf,01fe6c3bb5f28bd94df8afd595d8117d60aa259fc9336738ff0078dba1864e6f,True,5,"Output Direct Feedback Control for Takagi-Sugeno Fuzzy Systems * Wanhai Guo Zhihong Xiu Department of Command Control Research Center of Information and Control Dalian Naval Academy Dalian University of Technology Dalian, Liaoning Province, China Dalian, Liaoning Province, China dljyguo@126.com xzhdy@126.com * This work is partially supported by China Postdoctoral Science Foundation Grant 2005038255. Abstract - This paper presents a systematic design method of output direct feedback controllers for Takagi-Sugeno (T-S) fuzzy systems. The direct use of the output measurements to produce the input signal to the controller avoids the requirement for measuring or reconstructing the entire state vector so as to decrease the complexity of the controller. In order to use the structural information in the rule base to decrease the conservatism of the stability analysis, the standard fuzzy partition (SFP) is employed to the premise variables of fuzzy systems. New stability analysis and design me"
994d28d55eb8,frozen_450,/Users/baiyixin/Downloads/pdf_386_by_paper_id/994d28d55eb8.pdf,/Users/baiyixin/Documents/Survey - design knowledge/expanded_pdf_corpus_459_20260811/994d28d55eb8.pdf,a89ccb537fba476190019e174a0ea75bfd5fcc92c17a3cd9eed38950494e3db1,True,8,"From Human Factors to Human Actors to Human Crafters Monica Maceli College of Information Science and Technology Drexel University 3141 Chestnut St Philadelphia, PA 19104 USA mgm36@drexel.edu Michael Atwood College of Information Science and Technology Drexel University 3141 Chestnut St Philadelphia, PA 19104 USA atwood@drexel.edu ABSTRACT Meta-design theory emphasizes that future use can never be entirely anticipated at design time, as users shape their environments in response to emerging needs; systems should therefore be designed to adapt to future conditions in the hands of end users. For most of human history, all desig n was meta-design; designers were also users, and the environments of design and use were one and the same. Technology introduced a divide between the skilled producers and unskilled consumers of technology, and between design time and use time. In our inc reasingly complex technological environments, tomorrow‘s meta -designers must be able to anticipate the envir"
